# DS-0002: "Specify at least 1 USER command in Dockerfile with non-root user"
# Both Dockerfile.web and Dockerfile.worker intentionally have no static USER
# directive - they use the standard root-then-drop-privileges pattern (the
# same approach official images like postgres/mysql use): the container
# starts as root so its entrypoint script can fix permissions on ECS/Fargate
# volumes mounted after image build time (which do not inherit build-time
# chown/chmod), then exec's into the real process as a non-root user via
# su-exec. Trivy's static Dockerfile check cannot see that runtime privilege
# drop. Both containers do run as non-root in practice - verify with
# `ps aux` inside a running task, not by grepping the Dockerfile.
DS-0002
